<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Albanian Kingdom (1939-1943)</h1><p class="st-meta">1939 CE – 1943 CE · capital Tirana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Albania under Italian occupation, joined to Italy in a personal union under King Victor Emmanuel III and used as a base for the invasion of Greece.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> invaded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> on 7 April 1939, forcing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">King Zog</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albanian-kingdom">Albanian Kingdom</a> into exile. A constituent assembly summoned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a> offered the crown to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-iii">Victor Emmanuel III</a>, creating a personal union with Italy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shefqet-verlaci">Shefqet Vërlaci</a>, a large landowner and rival of Zog, became prime minister under an Italian lieutenant-general, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-jacomoni">Francesco Jacomoni</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Real power lay with Italian officials: Albania's army and foreign service were merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy's</a> and an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanian-fascist-party">Albanian Fascist Party</a> was created. Italy launched its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-persian-invasion-of-greece">invasion of Greece</a> from Albanian soil in October 1940, and after the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> in 1941 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> and western Macedonia were added, forming a Greater <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a>. Resistance grew, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha">Enver Hoxha's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/party-of-labour-of-albania">Communist Party</a>, founded in 1941.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> capitulated in September 1943, German troops occupied <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> and created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albanian-kingdom">Albanian Kingdom</a> (1943-1944), a nominally independent state under German control. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-emmanuel-iii">Victor Emmanuel III</a> formally renounced the Albanian crown in 1943, and the union with Italy was never restored.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/albanian-kingdom-1939-1943.jpg" alt="Albanian Kingdom (1939-1943)" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: F l a n k e r · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Albania_(1939-1943;_crowned).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1939 CE – 1943 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tirana</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Victor Emmanuel III, Shefqet Vërlaci, Francesco Jacomoni</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Orthodox and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a>, <a href="/countries/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, <a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Italian Albania, Italian protectorate of Albania</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1941&amp;focus=albanian-kingdom-1939-1943" aria-label="Albanian Kingdom (1939-1943) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5164 704 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Albanian Kingdom (1939-1943) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5484 960L5304 942M5484 960L5484 960"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5484 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5484 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5484 960h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tirana. <a href="/atlas?year=1941&amp;f